// =============================================================================
// POWER GENERATORS UPDATE POLICY
// =============================================================================
// Purpose: Real-time ingestion from RawData to power_generators table
// Business Context: Engineering-001 - Power Network Analysis
// Data Source: RawData table where endpoint = 'getGenerators'
// Trigger: Every time new data arrives in RawData
// =============================================================================

// Drop existing policy if it exists
.drop table power_generators policy update

// Create the update policy for power_generators using the parse_generators_data function
.alter table power_generators policy update
```
[
    {
        "IsEnabled": true,
        "Source": "RawData",
        "Query": "parse_generators_data()",
        "IsTransactional": false,
        "ManagedIdentity": null,
        "PropagateIngestionProperties": false
    }
]
```

// =============================================================================
// POLICY EXPLANATION
// =============================================================================
// This update policy:
// 1. Uses the parse_generators_data() function for data transformation
// 2. Provides clean separation of concerns (policy vs. parsing logic)
// 3. Enables easier maintenance and testing of parsing logic
// 4. Allows reuse of parsing logic in other contexts
// 5. Simplifies policy definition and readability
// 
// The parse_generators_data() function handles:
// - Filtering RawData for 'getGenerators' endpoint
// - Parsing JSON data structure
// - Extracting generator information from the data array
// - Transforming and calculating derived fields
// - Handling missing or null values with appropriate defaults
// - Converting data types to match table schema
// - Adding ingestion timestamp for audit trail
// =============================================================================

// =============================================================================
// MONITORING AND MAINTENANCE
// =============================================================================
// Monitor policy status:
// .show table power_generators policy update

// Check policy performance:
// .show table power_generators policy update statistics

// Disable policy if needed:
// .alter table power_generators policy update 
//   '[{"IsEnabled": false, "Source": "RawData", "Query": "...", "IsTransactional": false}]'

// View recent ingestion:
// power_generators
// | where ingestion_time >= ago(1h)
// | summarize count() by bin(ingestion_time, 1m)
// | order by ingestion_time desc

// =============================================================================
// PERFORMANCE CONSIDERATIONS
// =============================================================================
// 1. Policy processes data in real-time as it arrives
// 2. JSON parsing can be CPU intensive for large datasets
// 3. Consider batching for high-frequency updates
// 4. Monitor for ingestion lag and processing errors
// 5. Use appropriate data types to minimize storage overhead
// =============================================================================

// =============================================================================
// ERROR HANDLING
// =============================================================================
// Common issues and solutions:
// 1. JSON parsing errors: Check data format and add error handling
// 2. Data type conversion errors: Use safe conversion functions
// 3. Missing fields: Provide default values or handle nulls
// 4. Policy disabled: Check policy status and re-enable if needed
// 5. Ingestion lag: Monitor table ingestion statistics
// =============================================================================

// Test the policy with a sample query using the function
// parse_generators_data()
// | where timestamp >= ago(1h)
// | take 5
// | project 
//     timestamp,
//     server,
//     generator_id,
//     generator_name,
//     generator_class,
//     power_production_potential,
//     current_production,
//     production_efficiency

